and human papillomavirus (HPV) infection: no evidence of a viral etiology in a group of Swiss women</article-title><source>Breast</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>172</fpage><lpage>177</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Breast||16|172||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17088061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Houten</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Snijders</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Brekel</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kummer</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Meijer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van Leeuwen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Denkers</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Smeele</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Snow</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Brakenhoff</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biological evidence that human papillomaviruses are etiologically involved in a subgroup of head and neck squamous cell carcinomas</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>93</volume><supplement>2</supplement><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||93|232||bib17|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11410871</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Widschwendter</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Brunhuber</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiedemair</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mueller-Holzner</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Marth</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-titl